      {
        "id": "p15-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Draw a histogram.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Classes $150$–$159$, $160$–$169$, $170$–$179$, $180$–$189$, $190$–$199$ have frequencies $2,2,10,10,3$ respectively.",
          "worked": "Count the leaves in each stem row. The five class frequencies are $2,2,10,10,3$, totalling $27$. Draw touching bars for these equal-width classes with frequency on the vertical axis.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p15-q4-histogram-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 15 p15-q4-histogram-solution\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1.7cm,y=0.38cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\foreach \\y in {2,4,6,8,10,12}{\\draw[line width=0.25pt] (0,\\y)--(5,\\y);}\n\\draw[line width=0.5pt] (0,12)--(0,0)--(5,0);\n\\foreach \\y in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (-0.05,\\y)--(0,\\y);\\node[left] at (-0.05,\\y){\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\y\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (0,0) rectangle (1,2);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (1,0) rectangle (2,2);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (2,0) rectangle (3,10);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (3,0) rectangle (4,10);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (4,0) rectangle (5,3);\n\\foreach \\x/\\lab/\\row in {0.5/{150--159}/-0.8,1.5/{160--169}/-3.2,2.5/{170--179}/-0.8,3.5/{180--189}/-3.2,4.5/{190--199}/-0.8}{\\draw[line width=0.25pt] (\\x,-0.15)--(\\x,\\row);\\node[anchor=north] at (\\x,\\row){\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\lab\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\node[rotate=90] at (-1.15,6){Frequency};\n\\node[anchor=north] at (2.5,-6){Data value};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 130,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 15,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 4(a); answer page 83, Exercise 18C question 4(a)",
                "description": "Histogram with five touching, equal-width classes and frequencies 2, 2, 10, 10, 3. Unfilled bars retain all frequency information.",
                "mathematics": "Class boundaries 149.5,159.5,169.5,179.5,189.5,199.5; frequencies 2,2,10,10,3.",
                "answerVisibility": "solution-only"
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find $Q_1$, the median, $Q_3$ and the IQR.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$Q_1=173$, median $=179$, $Q_3=187$, IQR $=14$.",
          "worked": "There are $27$ ordered values, so the median is the 14th value, $179$. Omit this value when splitting the data into two groups of $13$. Each quartile is the 7th value of its group.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}Q_1&=173\\\\Q_3&=187\\\\\\text{IQR}&=187-173\\\\\\text{IQR}&=14\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 42
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Draw the boxplot.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Whiskers at $156$ and $193$; box from $173$ to $187$; median at $179$. No outliers.",
          "worked": "The five-number summary is $156,173,179,187,193$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Lower fence}&=173-1.5\\times14\\\\\\text{Lower fence}&=152\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=187+1.5\\times14\\\\\\text{Upper fence}&=208\\end{align*}$$\n\nAll values lie within the fences. Draw the box from $173$ to $187$, the median at $179$, and whiskers extending to $156$ and $193$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p15-q4-boxplot-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 15 p15-q4-boxplot-solution\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.18cm,y=0.8cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\draw[line width=0.5pt] (150,0)--(200,0);\n\\foreach \\x in {150,155,160,165,170,175,180,185,190,195,200}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (\\x,0)--(\\x,0.12);}\n\\foreach \\x/\\row in {150/-0.2,155/-1.2,160/-0.2,165/-1.2,170/-0.2,175/-1.2,180/-0.2,185/-1.2,190/-0.2,195/-1.2,200/-0.2}{\\draw[line width=0.25pt] (\\x,-0.05)--(\\x,\\row);\\node[anchor=north] at (\\x,\\row){\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}\\x\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (156,1)--(173,1);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (173,0.7) rectangle (187,1.3);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (179,0.7)--(179,1.3);\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt] (187,1)--(193,1);\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 125,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 15,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 4(c); answer page 83, Exercise 18C question 4(c)",
                "description": "Unfilled horizontal boxplot on a labelled scale from 150 to 200, with no outliers.",
                "mathematics": "Minimum 156, lower quartile 173, median 179, upper quartile 187, maximum 193.",
                "answerVisibility": "solution-only"
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "p15-q4-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Comment on the shape of the histogram and the boxplot.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Both displays suggest a negative skew, with a longer tail towards the smaller values.",
          "worked": "The histogram has two low-frequency classes below its two tallest bars, but only one above them. The boxplot's lower whisker has length $173-156=17$, compared with $193-187=6$ for the upper whisker. These longer lower tails suggest negative skew.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
